; Control keys: 8 (half-row index, bit mask) pairs
;
; Pair n gives the key for control bit n (see #R$A2CF); #R$A271 tests each pair against the row buffer at #R$A2D3. The
; values here are the defaults (QAOP); #R$A3B9 overwrites the first four pairs when the player redefines the keys and
; #R$A336 copies the JUMP pair into the fifth. Each pair is +0 byte: half-row index 0-7 (port high bytes $FE, $FD,
; $FB, $F7, $EF, $DF, $BF, $7F), +1 byte: bit mask of the key in that half-row (bit 0 is the key nearest the edge).
; .
; The last three pairs are fixed: T, R and Y.
@label=ControlKeys
g$A2BF DEFB $05,$01  ; bit 0 RIGHT: P
@label=KeyLeft
 $A2C1 DEFB $05,$02  ; bit 1 LEFT: O
@label=KeyCrouch
 $A2C3 DEFB $01,$01  ; bit 2 CROUCH: A
@label=KeyJump
 $A2C5 DEFB $02,$01  ; bit 3 JUMP: Q
@label=KeyJumpCopy
 $A2C7 DEFB $02,$01  ; bit 4 JUMP again: a copy of the pair above (the Kempston fire bit is bit 4)
@label=KeyWarp
 $A2C9 DEFB $02,$10  ; bit 5 fixed: T, the debug room warp (only if the cheat is on)
@label=KeyAbortR
 $A2CB DEFB $02,$08  ; bit 6 fixed: R, with Y it ends the game
@label=KeyAbortY
 $A2CD DEFB $05,$10  ; bit 7 fixed: Y
